  "instructions": [
    "Rinse the rice in a fine strainer until the water runs mostly clear. Cook it in a small pot with the water and a pinch of salt if you want rice on the side, or skip to the next step to use the rice in the curry pot.",
    "Heat the coconut oil in a large deep skillet or Dutch oven over medium heat. Add the onion and cook for 4 minutes, until soft.",
    "Stir in the garlic, ginger, curry powder, turmeric, and kosher salt. Cook for 1 minute, until fragrant.",
    "Add the diced tomatoes with their juice and the coconut milk. Stir well and bring to a gentle simmer.",
    "Simmer for 8 minutes, stirring now and then, until the sauce thickens slightly.",
    "Add the shrimp in a single layer. Cover and cook for 4 to 5 minutes, until the shrimp are pink and curled and opaque in the center.",
    "Stir in the cilantro. Spoon the curry over the cooked rice and serve hot."
  ],
